    "text": "(F. Lisi, L. Sabatini). Let G be a non-trivial finite group and let p1 , . . . , pk be\nthe distinct prime divisors of |G|. For each i, let Hi be a Sylow pi -subgroup of G. Is\nit true that there exists an element x ∈ G such that for all i the subgroup Hi ∩ Hix is\ninclusion-minimal in {Hi ∩ Hig : g ∈ G}?                                  T. C. Burness",
